    "city": "sanaa",
    "climate": "highland",
    "vernacular": "High-altitude (2,250 m) arid city. The Old City is a dense cluster of 5-9 storey tower houses: dark basalt or stone lower floors, fired-brick upper floors, white lime/gypsum friezes and window frames, semicircular stained-glass fanlights (qamariya), flat roofs with stepped parapets and a top-floor mafraj room. The modern city is 3-6 storey concrete-frame blocks in sandy render, flat roofs with rooftop water tanks, high compound walls, shop fronts with roll shutters and very little street planting.",
    "wallColours": [
      "#a0583a",
      "#7a4630",
      "#d8c6a2",
      "#f1ece0",
      "#c9b48e",
      "#6b6864",
