      "metal-sheet"
    ],
    "ground": "paving",
    "vegetation": [
      "acacia",
      "palm",
      "broadleaf"
    ],
    "ornament": "White lime and gypsum geometric friezes outlining every window and storey line; qamariya semicircular fanlights of coloured glass in white tracery; stepped crenellated parapets; black basalt courses at the base; carved wooden doors with brass rings; brick laid in decorative patterns. Modern buildings echo these with white-painted window surrounds and green, red and white banding on mosques.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_City_of_Sana%27a",
        "what": "multi-floor houses with flat roofs, friezes and carved frames, stained-glass windows, maqshama gardens, clay walls"
      },
      {
        "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bab_al-Yaman",
        "what": "surrounding houses of baked brick decorated and waterproofed with lime plaster and qadad; stained-glass fanlights; main gate of the fortified wall"
      },
      {
        "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dar_al-Hajar",
        "what": "basalt lower floors plus fired-brick upper floors, seven floors on rock, valley setting with doum palms"
      },
      {
        "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al_Saleh_Mosque",
        "what": "modern Yemeni mosque in red, white and black limestone with black basalt"
      }
    ]
